# Internal records · `guide:acts:records`

**Section (Acts)** · `sec:acts:area-acts` {{ row('org.peer-network.testing.claim-areas', owner='RECORDS', area='acts').stake }} The first slice implements local validation under (`[ROOT-sig:design:records]`) and (`[ROOT-model:design:accepted-act]`); it does not certify authentication, formation, membership, family endpoint typing or a standing result.

**Definition (Structural identity)** · `def:acts:identity` An ActId consists of its exact public author identifier, author-local sequence and exact family name. An EdgeId consists of its parent ActId and Binary, A or T role. Authoritative position, finalization epoch and removal facts are not identifier fields. Equal endpoints do not collapse distinct edge identities.

**Definition (References)** · `def:acts:references` PublicReference is an act, edge or exact namespace/name identity. The supplied set is previously accepted history, so a batch act already in it refuses as a duplicate. resolve_public_reference takes ValidatedRecords and distinguishes History from Batch, refusing missing or malformed required queries. Tombstones never erase these identities. No database or codec is consulted.

**Definition (Projection ownership)** · `def:acts:projection` A Binary layout owns one Binary structural leg; a Paired layout owns A and T together. Neither leg owns a removal state: any candidate leg removal field refuses. RemovableProjections carries the act's independent content and dependency facts; a tombstone must follow the act's authoritative position. Dependency edge status derives from this act-owned dependency fact, never from a co-leg. Both structural legs and immutable protocol identities survive a dependency tombstone, following (`[ROOT-amend:design:act-removal-facts]`). This snapshot validator admits no mutation or resurrection operation.

**Definition (Structural body)** · `def:acts:body` The first local body representation declares its projection layout and named exact integer quantities with explicit units and vintages. Validation preserves these fields without conversion and refuses empty or duplicate quantity names and empty units. This bounded integer carrier is not the later family census, rational valuation or external byte profile; those contracts must supply their own types before use. No codec or canonical encoding is assigned here under (`[ROOT-amend:design:bite-one-internal-envelopes]`).

**Definition (Act carrier)** · `def:acts:carrier` CandidateAct is the complete candidate: identifier, author, family, structural body, structural legs and separate act-owned removable projections, immutable protocol references, public authentication evidence, finalization epoch and authoritative position. The identity is the sole representation of author and family. Nonempty authentication evidence is retained as public content; its authenticity is not inferred from that local check.

**Definition (Local validation)** · `def:acts:validation` validate_record validates the complete batch and returns a borrowed ValidatedRecords view. Duplicate act or edge identities, missing required references, missing co-legs and inconsistent local fields return distinct ValidationError variants. The view returns whole acts without cloning, flattening, sorting by host position or mutating input. Borrowing keeps the validated snapshot immutable. Declaration identities and effective boundaries are validated before as-of selection. ValidationError derives thiserror::Error and remains exhaustive while unpublished; InvalidCause makes local refusals exhaustively distinguishable. Every public operation is labelled and accounted at every observation level; payloads are captured only at trace. The executable owns bootstrap. There are no optional features and no production codec or graph dependency.


**Definition (Opaque declarations)** · `def:acts:declarations` DeclarationId contains one namespace, name and edition; Declaration retains its announcement and effective boundaries without a payload. Validation rejects empty keys, duplicate identities, simultaneous successors and effect before announcement. select_effective_declaration takes only ValidatedRecords and selects by effective boundary, not edition number or vector order, preserving old answers at old boundaries under (`[ROOT-amend:design:bite-one-declaration-selection]`). Declaration contents remain in bite 2.

**Amendment (First slice evidence)** · `amend:acts:first-slice-evidence` The supported premises for (`[ROOT-gate:design:bite-1]`) are: Finite structural, act-removal, accepted-history reference and opaque as-of declaration fixtures, plus the records runtime comparison; no boundary assembler, closure partition, shared suite, generator tier or declaration payload semantics is claimed. Their test-site evidence is (`claim:acts:identity-is-structural`), (`claim:acts:complete-acts-are-counted-once`), (`claim:acts:duplicates-refuse-and-parallel-identities-survive`), (`claim:acts:both-co-legs-are-required`), (`claim:acts:protocol-references-outlive-dependency-removal`), (`claim:acts:invalid-local-fields-refuse`), (`claim:acts:removal-belongs-to-act-projections`), (`claim:acts:references-resolve-against-accepted-history`), (`claim:acts:opaque-editions-preserve-as-of-selection`), (`claim:acts:ambiguous-declaration-histories-refuse`), (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:records-entry-is-observed-without-changing-results]`). The gate remains held for the remaining steps in (`[ROOT-amend:design:bite-one-step-plan]`); previously accepted history is supplied by the caller and no partition algorithm or family formation verdict is inferred.
